# =============================================================================
# Caddy — tenant STACK ingress (caddy-stack-ingress). ADDITIVE + PROFILE-GATED.
# nginx keeps every PLATFORM vhost; Caddy owns ONLY the stack hostnames
# (*.apps.${BASE_DOMAIN} / *.services… + tenant custom domains) — design D6.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. scripts/caddy-entrypoint.sh renders it (busybox awk,
# not envsubst — stock caddy:2-alpine ships no gettext), mirroring the role of
# the platform nginx entrypoint (its my_nginx_proxy container, full stack). The two big blocks
# below are computed by the entrypoint from ${STACK_TLS_ISSUER} (design D3):
#   - CADDY_GLOBAL_TLS_BLOCK : issuer/ACME + on-demand config inside global opts
#   - CADDY_STACK_SITE       : the stack ingress site block
# Both are EMPTY when the issuer is unset/invalid → the edge stays INERT (no
# 443 listener, no ACME fires unbidden). Only the loopback admin API and the
# internal health endpoint are always present.
# =============================================================================
{
	# Admin API on loopback only. The BYO watch-and-reload step (Group 5, NOT
	# implemented here) POSTs /load to this to hot-swap a rotated cert with no
	# redeploy. Kept off any published port so it is never reachable off-box.
	admin 127.0.0.1:2019

	# Rendered from ${STACK_TLS_ISSUER} by caddy-entrypoint.sh. Empty ⇒ inert.
${CADDY_GLOBAL_TLS_BLOCK}
}

# Always-on internal health endpoint for the compose healthcheck. Deliberately
# independent of issuer state so an INERT edge (no issuer) still reports healthy
# — the profile being up with no issuer must not look "unhealthy". Internal
# port only; never published.
:2021 {
	respond /healthz "ok" 200
	respond 404
}

# Stack ingress site — rendered from ${STACK_TLS_ISSUER} by caddy-entrypoint.sh.
# Empty when the issuer is unset/invalid (edge inert). When present it binds
# Caddy's OWN https port (see the compose port publish; nginx keeps its own
# host ports and Caddy never touches them) and answers only the stack
# wildcards + custom domains.
${CADDY_STACK_SITE}
